<title>HONG KONG: Insolvency cases in Hong Kong rise in 1996/97.</title>
<headline>Insolvency cases in Hong Kong rise in 1996/97.</headline>
<dateline>HONG KONG 1997-04-24</dateline>
<text>
<p>Hong Kong's Official Receiver's office said on Thursday the total number of new court insolvencies had increased to 1,119 in 1996/97 (April-March) from 1,013 in 1995/96.</p>
<p>There were 557 new compulsory company liquidations in 1996/97, representing less than one percent of the 58,010 new companies incorporated during the year, the office said in a statement.</p>
<p>The corresponding figures in 1995/96 were 514 and 1.5 percent, it said.</p>
<p>-- Hong Kong newsroom (852) 2843 6441</p>
</text>
